cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "sageRecon: a Sage-based proteomics reconnaissance tool"
abstract: >-
  A reconnaissance tool for unfamiliar bottom-up proteomics data. It runs one
  wide open search plus one semi-enzymatic confirmation pass, then reports which
  modifications are present, what the digest looks like, and what mass
  tolerances the data supports, before a production search is configured. The
  open search assumes no fixed modification, including carbamidomethyl on
  cysteine, so the observed cysteine chemistry is reported rather than presumed.
